  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>3804708ddafbe942b12fb847ef833dc8</srcmd5>
    <version>5.15.0</version>
    <time>1786461242</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 5.15.0.

Also fixes the FTBFS/import breakage the package has had in Factory since
python-tokenizers 0.23.1 landed (it currently fails to build on all arches):
upstream transformers pins tokenizers to &lt;=0.23.0, but 0.23.0 was never
published as a stable release, so the only 0.23.x on PyPI - and the one in
Factory - is 0.23.1. The pin is enforced at import time by
dependency_versions_check.py, so 'import transformers' raised

  ImportError: tokenizers&gt;=0.22.0,&lt;=0.23.0 is required for a normal
  functioning of this module, but found tokenizers==0.23.1.

transformers-allow-tokenizers-0.23.1.patch widens the bound to &lt;0.24.0,
keeping the intent of the cap, and the Requires now declares that ceiling so
a future tokenizers 0.24 shows up as unresolvable rather than installing
cleanly and dying on import.

Upstream is aware (huggingface/transformers#47429, #45736) but has closed the
community PRs proposing exactly this change ('We'll handle tokenizers version
bumps internally'), so the fix stays downstream for now.

CVE-2025-6921 (boo#1250447): not affected, that ReDoS was fixed upstream in
4.53.0.

Built green locally for aarch64 against openSUSE:Factory:ARM/standard; rpmlint
4 badness (4x non-executable-script on upstream's shebanged library modules,
pre-existing and untouched to keep this update scoped to the fix).</comment>
    <requestid>1370545</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ea4b063152ce9c77903052afcbf7c3c1</srcmd5>
